From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: accept PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR on gen1

Streaming hosts ask the encoder for SPS/PPS in front of every IDR, so a
client can join, or recover, at any keyframe. VA-API drivers over V4L2
set V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR and give up when it fails.
Gen2 has the control; gen1 (SM8250) returns -EINVAL.

The gen1 firmware already does it. HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_SYNC_FRAME_
SEQUENCE_HEADER is one switch, a sequence header with every sync frame,
and HEADER_MODE_JOINED_WITH_1ST_FRAME (the default) turns it on. On
SM8250 every IDR asked for with FORCE_KEY_FRAME comes out with SPS and
PPS in front of it.

Add the cap to the gen1 encoder and turn the switch on when it is set,
whatever the header mode, as gen2 does. Nothing changes for a client
that leaves it at 0.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
index 073378e..de720c3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
@@ -661,14 +661,21 @@ int iris_set_profile_level_gen1(struct iris_inst *inst, enum platform_inst_fw_ca
 int iris_set_header_mode_gen1(struct iris_inst *inst, enum platform_inst_fw_cap_type cap_id)
 {
 	const struct iris_hfi_session_ops *hfi_ops = inst->hfi_session_ops;
+	u32 prepend_sps_pps = inst->fw_caps[PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR].value;
 	u32 header_mode = inst->fw_caps[cap_id].value;
 	u32 hfi_id = inst->fw_caps[cap_id].hfi_id;
 	u32 hfi_val;
 
-	if (header_mode == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE)
-		hfi_val = 0;
-	else
+	/*
+	 * Gen1 has a single switch: a sequence header with every sync frame.
+	 * Joined mode already turns it on, so prepending to each IDR is the
+	 * same setting.
+	 */
+	if (prepend_sps_pps ||
+	    header_mode == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_JOINED_WITH_1ST_FRAME)
 		hfi_val = 1;
+	else
+		hfi_val = 0;
 
 	return hfi_ops->session_set_property(inst, hfi_id,
 					 HFI_HOST_FLAGS_NONE,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
index b11a31e..2ed8d76 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
@@ -127,6 +127,13 @@ static const struct platform_inst_fw_cap inst_fw_cap_sm8250_enc[] = {
 		.flags = CAP_FLAG_OUTPUT_PORT | CAP_FLAG_MENU,
 		.set = iris_set_header_mode_gen1,
 	},
+	{
+		.cap_id = PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR,
+		.min = 0,
+		.max = 1,
+		.step_or_mask = 1,
+		.value = 0,
+	},
 	{
 		.cap_id = BITRATE,
 		.min = BITRATE_MIN,
